From 897c5de9c2d38f654a4219c5fb0631f29af8d64b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:41:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Delta 1.1.0: Claude accounts on the command center

The phone no longer holds a Claude login. It fetches short-lived access
tokens from the command center, which keeps every account and renews
them; an older install hands its own login over on first use.

- Chats lists the sessions of every account. New sessions start on the
  first account whose usage report shows room.
- When a session's account runs out, the foot of the transcript says
  until when and offers "Move to a new session". Moving stores the old
  session's whole history (every message, tool call and result) on the
  command center and starts a session on another account that is told
  to fetch it with delta resume. A message sent instead waits on the
  phone until the limit lifts.
- New Accounts tab: each account's 5-hour and weekly usage and resets.
- The APK bakes in only the command center login.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011uFtbcVnLGZ5q3jJCocSgk
